==English==

===Etymology===
* From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|condōno||forgive}}, {{m|la|con-||together}} + {{m|la|dōnāre||to give}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|əʊn|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|condon}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[forgive]], [[excuse]] or [[overlook]] (something).
#* {{quote-book|year=1963|author={{w|Margery Allingham}}|title={{w|The China Governess}}
|chapter=18|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL2004261W
|passage=‘Then the father has a great fight with his terrible conscience,’ said Munday with granite seriousness. ‘Should he make a row with the police&nbsp;[…]?&nbsp; Or should he say nothing about it and '''condone''' brutality for fear of appearing in the newspapers?}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[allow]], [[accept]] or [[permit]] (something).
# {{lb|en|transitive|legal}} To forgive (marital [[infidelity]] or other marital offense).

